WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:01.810
Hi, everyone.

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.600
And welcome to MIT's
2020 Online Commencement.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.790
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:10.000
Only when we are aware that
our time is nearing an end

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.670
do we actually make the
most of the time left

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.550
and live in the moment.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.400
So I urge you all,
Class of 2020,

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.520
to live the rest of your lives
with the mindset you likely

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.760
had when you were told we had
a week left in our college

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.140
careers.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.170
Take risks, go all
in, shoot your shot,

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:32.009
find the things that will make
you feel fulfilled every day.

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:34.877
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.587
[INAUDIBLE]

00:00:43.587 --> 00:00:45.335
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.720
As you strive to hack
the world, please

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.250
try to heal the world too.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.450
Please help us respond
to this brutal pandemic

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:04.120
with wisdom, foresight,
compassion, and science.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.340
I want you to
promise me one thing,

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.020
promise me that you
will be the last class,

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.620
the last class to miss
a commencement because

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:12.440
of a pandemic.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:16.750
The last class to miss a
commencement because of war.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:19.300
The last class to
miss a commencement

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.710
because of climate change,
unrest, tyranny, extremism,

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:26.920
active shooters,
intolerance, and apathy.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.130
Batman and Superman are not
coming to save the world.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:32.040
It will be up to you.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.690
But never, never in my life
have I been so confident

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.180
that the fate of the
world is in good hands.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.140
Go forth and be the
heroes we need you to be.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:48.540
So get some rest graduates,
and then get started.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.267
There is a lot of
work in front of us.

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:53.130
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.650
I ask you all now to
raise your right hand

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.450
and turn your brass rat.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]MIT

